<github-data-json>
{
  "title": "Privacy matching: decode JSON \\/ in private strings and register the \\/ spelling of credentials",
  "body": "Slice (b) of #880. It starts after #916 (a), because both edit src/gates/private.ts.\n\n## Problem\nJSON output may escape `/` as `\\/`. Neither matcher decodes that spelling:\n- The private matcher's `decoded` (src/gates/private.ts ~150) decodes percent and `\\uXXXX` escapes only. `host\\/path.example` doesn't match the entry `host/path.example`.\n- Credential redaction registers each secret's raw spelling and its `JSON.stringify` spelling (src/util/proc.ts ~1235, `registerCredential`). `JSON.stringify` doesn't escape `/`. `token\\/with-slash` in JSON-escaped output isn't redacted when `token/with-slash` is registered.\n\n## Requirements\n- **Credentials:** when a secret contains `/`, also register the JSON spelling with every `/` written as `\\/`. This is one more variant in the existing Aho-Corasick matcher (src/util/credential-matcher.ts). Don't decode the text, and don't build offset maps for it.\n- **Private strings:** decode `\\/` (any run of backslashes before `/`, like the existing `\\\\+u` handling) to `/` in `decoded`.\n- **Make `decoded` linear.** Its `\\\\+u([0-9a-f]{4})` replace is unanchored, so on a long run of backslashes with no `u` it rescans the run from every position. Review of #921 measured `privateMatches` on main on `\"diagnostic \" + \"\\\\\".repeat(n) + \"!\"`: 71, 292, 1,149 and 4,620 ms for n = 25k, 50k, 100k and 200k. A PR's diff text reaches it through the audit. Replace the `\\uXXXX` and `\\/` handling with one forward pass that consumes each backslash run once, with the same output as today's `\\uXXXX` decoding plus the new `\\/`.\n- Keep one implementation of each matcher. Nothing else changes.\n- **Hot path:** both functions run on gate output. Report one before-and-after table in the PR at production size:\n  - workload: 5 MiB of realistic logs and JSON, once with occasional `\\/` and once without;\n  - 0, 50, 200 and 600 registered random credentials, with eight private entries;\n  - median total ms and worst event-loop stall, for `redactCredentials` and `privateMatches`;\n  - use scripts/benchmark-credential-redaction.ts or extend it.\n  Neither function may get more than 10% slower than main on either workload. A previous attempt, #909, roughly doubled both: avoid whole-text offset maps.\n\n## Tests\nEach fails without the change:\n- a registered `abc/def-ghijkl-credential` written as `abc\\/def-ghijkl-credential` inside a JSON string is redacted by `redactCredentials`;\n- the same through one end-to-end path: stored gate event output;\n- `privateMatches` matches `host\\/path.example` against the entry `host/path.example`, and `\\\\\\/` runs decode the same way;\n- the same through `privateOutputData`, as MCP results use it.\n- the backslash-run family with n = 400,000 and a non-matching entry returns no match (on main it takes about 18 s; assert the result, not the time);\n- the new pass gives the same output as today's regex on every string up to 6 characters over `\\ u / 0 a f z !`, plus a random sample of longer strings.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Other JSON escapes such as `\\\"` or `\\\\` in the middle of a value.\n- Truncation and check ordering: #918 and #919.\n- Adversarial encodings (#335).\n\nBudget: about 40 source lines plus tests and the benchmark table.\n"
}
</github-data-json>
